if you simply ran out of things to do in  vanilla destiny to its first DLC  expansion curse of Osiris adds a few new  activities for you to take on but aside  from the short but fun raid lair almost  all the new stuff in cursive Osiris the  story missions strikes crucible Maps  adventures and weapons don't add  anything substantial or interesting to  destiny to to make it worth revisiting  cursive Osiris picks up right after the  end of the base game's campaign as far  as your level goes you could go directly  from the end of the red war story to  cursive Osiris's campaign which requires  a power level of 200 to 220 without  having to grind much in between for  newcomers or PC players who've had less  time with the game it's a comfortable  bridge for leveling up between the lower  level vanilla content in the high level  in-game activity is like the nightfall  those in-game activities are a different  story but we'll get to that in a bit as  a result though curse of Osiris is story  missions feel like filler the campaign  sets up an enormous undertaking against  the vex with infinite timelines and  computer simulations and the mysterious  Warlock Osiris mixed up in it all but  with the torso our run time the missions  rushed through the interesting concepts  and usher you into a simple final battle  that is essentially scripted it's also  not enough time to fully understand  Osiris as a character which is  disappointing considering he's only ever  been mentioned in destiny lore before  now if I don't stop the vex there won't  be anything to come back to I'm doing  this for the part of us  the beautiful and varied infinite forest  of vex creation designed to simulate  timelines and their infinite  permutations is the most interesting  addition to the expansion but even then  the story doesn't task you with  exploring it instead shepherding you  through areas to find codes and things  that smarter NPCs can use to pinpoint  your next destination for you scanning  other than the infinite forest the new  destination mercury is simply  uninteresting to explore it's a small  circular map with one new public event  to try out a new vendor and a handful of  chests and loss sectors foundation of  exploration established in the base game  is still good here having a variety of  options to choose from does make things  feel less repetitive but it feels like  busywork with little to do at the  highest level that extends to the new  strikes which are almost direct copies  of two of the story missions nothing  more than another way to kill time the  biggest problem with curse of Osiris is  that it locks the hardest activities  including the prestige nightfall in the  prestige raid behind its new power level  cap the recommended power for those  activities is 3:30 which you can't reach  if you don't have the curse of Osiris  DLC so if you don't get the DLC you  suddenly don't have access to something  you used to be able to do it's also  frustrating if you do get curse of  Osiris because the higher level  requirement doesn't fundamentally change  these activities new heroic adventures  add nightfall style modifiers to the  adventures on Mercury but those missions  aren't begging to be replayed the main  incentive to do it at all is to unlock a  lost prophecy quest from the npc brother  Vance which is one of the most tedious  consumable gathering chores in all of  destiny 2 if you do manage to gather ten  of the necessary item through repeating  public events and finding chests you  unlock the forge where you can craft  legendary vex weapons but for anyone  besides the most dedicated players  there's no compelling reason to do all  of this unless you want to redo old  missions on hardware difficulties in  order to get loot to use when you do  them again while some of the new loot is  worth collecting my favorites of the  ones I've found are a legendary  automatic scout rifle and the broken but  ridiculously fun prometheus lens exotic  you'll likely get a lot of duplicate  before you get anything you actually  want to use because the main reward for  everything you do is shiny new loot the  frustratingly high drop rate of  duplicates makes grinding more  disappointing than satisfying the  gunplay feels as great as ever though so  it can be fun to experiment with new  weapons but it's not enough to sustain  an expansion that adds little outside of  extra busy work the raid layer while  shorter than a typical Destiny's raid is  the one late-game addition that's worth  trying eater of worlds is set on  leviathan the setting of destiny two's  first raid with a different boss and  separate areas to explore it features a  mix of destiny style puzzles including a  platforming sequence and fun with orbs  using careful teamwork to solve puzzles  is rewarding in ways the story and  simple strikes can't be and combining  that with the right loadout and strong  shooting skills showcases what destiny  could be but in almost every respect  cursive Osiris doesn't elevate destiny  to beyond what it was it launched  especially for lapse players the same  old activities reskin for an  unremarkable new setting feel more like  chores than ever and the interesting  ideas in the infinite forest aren't it  all use their potentials there's still  some fun to be had in finding new  weapons and maybe tackling the raid lair  but reaching that point is so tedious  that it hardly feels worth doing there's  something else in here with me  and coded holo images big ones  definitely vex  look I can't decrypt those files or open  the gate we need backup  we need Ike aura good idea right
 

